  "question": {
    "text": "A radioactive nucleus can decay by two different processes. Half-life for the first process is <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>3</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>0</mn></math>&nbsp;hours while it is <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>4</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>5</mn></math> hours for the second process. The effective halflife of the nucleus will be"
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>3</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>75</mn></math> hours",
      "is_correct": false
    },
    {
      "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>0</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>56</mn></math> hours",
      "is_correct": false
    },
    {
      "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>0</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>26</mn></math> hours",
      "is_correct": false
    },
    {
      "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>1</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>80</mn></math> hours",
      "is_correct": true
    }
  ],
  "correct_answer": [
    "D"
  ],
  "solution": {
    "text": "<p>Here the particle is decayed by two processes with decay constant&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>&#955;</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></math>&nbsp;and&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>&#955;</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></math>.</p><p>&nbsp;&nbsp;<img src=\"assets\\st0061_37fa2965bd06.png\" style=\"width: 170px; height: 135px;\" /></p><p>Radioactive decay rate is directly proportional to number of nucleus present at any time, so total rate of decay is&nbsp;</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfrac><mrow><mo>d</mo><mi>A</mi></mrow><mrow><mo>d</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></mfrac><mo>-</mo><mfenced><mrow><mo>-</mo><msub><mi>&#955;</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mi>A</mi></mrow></mfenced><mo>+</mo><mfenced><mrow><mo>-</mo><msub><mi>&#955;</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mi>A</mi></mrow></mfenced></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8658;</mo><mfrac><mrow><mo>d</mo><mi>A</mi></mrow><mrow><mo>d</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mo>-</mo><mfenced><mrow><msub><mi>&#955;</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>&#955;</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow></mfenced><mi>A</mi></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8658;</mo><msub><mi>&#955;</mi><mrow><mi>eff</mi><mo>&#160;</mo></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>&#955;</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>&#955;</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8658;</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>ln</mi><mn>2</mn></mrow><msub><mfenced><msub><mi>t</mi><mstyle displaystyle=\"true\"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mstyle></msub></mfenced><mi>eff</mi></msub></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>ln</mi><mn>2</mn></mrow><msub><mfenced><msub><mi>t</mi><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac></msub></mfenced><mn>1</mn></msub></mfrac><mo>+</mo><mfrac><mfenced><mrow><mi>ln</mi><mn>2</mn></mrow></mfenced><msub><mfenced><msub><mi>t</mi><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac></msub></mfenced><mn>2</mn></msub></mfrac></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8658;</mo><msub><mfenced><msub><mi>t</mi><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac></msub></mfenced><mrow><mi>off</mi><mo>&#160;</mo></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>4</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>5</mn><mo>&#215;</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow><mrow><mn>7</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>5</mn></mrow></mfrac></math> hours <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>8</mn></math>&nbsp;hours</p>"
  }
